      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like youre kind of dismissing the prosperity side. like, if the economy as a whole gets bigger and prices for goods go down for everyone, isn't that still a win for the working class too? it seems like you're leaning hard into the idea that it's a failure. can you just address if there's actually any legitimate way to see it as a success for laborers, or is the 'failure' angle just the only way to look at it realistically?",
